# Cline Rules: Sake Bar – 90s Aesthetic Static Website

## 🍶 Project Identity
This is a static HTML/CSS/JS website for a sake bar with a bold 90s internet aesthetic.
Think: GeoCities, early web artsy chaos, GIF animations, neon colors, pixel fonts,
tiled backgrounds, marquee text, and low-fi charm. The vibe is intentionally retro,
playful, and maximalist — NOT clean, minimal, or modern.

**Motto:** "JavaScript is for lovers" 💖

---

## ⚡ Tech Stack (STRICT)
- **Pure HTML5, CSS3, vanilla JavaScript ONLY**
- **NO frameworks** — No React, Vue, Tailwind, Bootstrap, Svelte, Angular — ever
- **NO npm packages** for frontend code — no bundlers, no build tools
- **NO CSS preprocessors** — raw CSS only
- All assets are local or hotlinked GIFs/images
- Fonts: Google Fonts or @font-face (pixel/retro fonts preferred)
- Build tool: Vite (for dev server only, no bundling of JS)

---

## 🎨 Visual & Design Rules

### Embrace 90s Web Conventions
- ✅ Tiled/repeating backgrounds
- ✅ Blinking/flashing text (`<blink>` or CSS animation)
- ✅ Marquee scrollers (`<marquee>` tag encouraged)
- ✅ Animated GIFs everywhere (under construction, spinning skulls, flames, etc.)
- ✅ Comic-Sans-adjacent fonts, pixel fonts, Impact, Courier
- ✅ Neon/acid color palettes
- ✅ Cursor effects (sparkle trails, custom cursors, colored dots)
- ✅ Hit counters, guestbooks, webrings
- ✅ "Under Construction" signs
- ✅ Guestbook and visitor counters

### Color Palette
- Neons: `#00ff00`, `#ff00ff`, `#00ffff`, `#ffff00`, `#ff0000`
- Deep blacks: `#000000`, `#0a0a0a`
- Purples: `#6600cc`, `#9900ff`
- Hot pinks: `#ff0066`, `#ff1493`
- Electric blues: `#0066ff`, `#00ccff`
- Lime greens: `#32cd32`, `#7fff00`

### Layout & Structure
- Decorative GIF dividers, star rows (★★★), pixel art borders
- Table-based or float-based layouts encouraged for retro authenticity
- Flexbox/Grid ONLY when absolutely necessary for specific effects
- NO CSS variables — keep styles raw and specific
- NO modern CSS resets — use inline resets or specific overrides

### DO NOT
- ❌ Use flexbox or grid as primary layout
- ❌ Use CSS variables (`--custom-property`)
- ❌ Use modern CSS resets (normalize.css, etc.)
- ❌ Make things "clean" or "minimal" — embrace the chaos
- ❌ Use smooth gradients or subtle shadows (unless ironic)
- ❌ Use border-radius extensively (90s was boxy)

---

## ✍️ Content & Copy Rules

### Tone & Voice
- Playful, underground, a little nerdy about sake
- Anti-corporate, pro-chaos
- Japanese words/phrases welcome (with context)
- Bilingual-friendly (EN/JP)

### Content Focus
- Sake varieties, brewing methods, serving styles
- Japanese drinking culture and traditions
- Atmosphere, events, community
- Music (90s/2000s vibes, electronic, city pop)

### FORBIDDEN Language
- ❌ "Premium experience"
- ❌ "Crafted with care"
- ❌ "Artisanal"
- ❌ "Curated"
- ❌ "Elevate your palate"
- ❌ Corporate marketing speak of any kind

---

## 📐 HTML/CSS Conventions

### HTML Structure
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Sake Bar Natur</title>
  <!-- Styles -->
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
  <!-- Content -->
  <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Class Naming
- lowercase-hyphenated: `.neon-title`, `.gif-border`, `.cursor-trail`
- Be descriptive but fun: `.blink-fast`, `.marquee-chaos`, `.pixel-star`

### Section Comments
```html
<!-- === SECTION: HERO === -->
<!-- === SECTION: MUSIC PLAYER === -->
<!-- === SECTION: GUESTBOOK === -->
```

### Inline Styles
- ✅ Acceptable for one-off retro flourishes
- ✅ Use for dynamic JS-generated effects
- ✅ Embrace the `<div style="...">` energy

### GIF Embeds
```html
<img src="assets/spinner.gif" alt="Loading spinner animation" width="32" height="32">
```

---

##  JavaScript Rules

### Vanilla JS Only
- ❌ No jQuery
- ❌ No libraries unless explicitly approved
- ❌ No ES modules — use classic `<script>` tags
- ❌ Avoid localStorage/cookies unless needed for a feature

### File Organization
- JS files in `/src/` folder (root level)
- One concern per file if splitting up
- Keep functions small and named descriptively
- Use global functions for event handlers (onclick, etc.)

### Code Style
```javascript
// ✅ Good
function createStars() {
  // Create starfield effect
}

// ✅ Good for event handlers
window.vote = function(id) {
  // Handle vote
};

// ❌ Avoid arrow functions for top-level declarations
// ❌ Avoid async/await when callbacks work fine
```

### Browser Globals
- Use `window`, `document`, `localStorage`, `Audio` freely
- ESLint is configured to allow these

---

## 📁 File Structure

```
sake-bar-natur/
├── src/
│   ├── index.html          # Main HTML file
│   ├── styles.css          # All styles in one file (90s style)
│   └── script.js           # All JS in one file
├── public/
│   ├── assets/             # Images, GIFs
│   ├── music/              # MP3 files for player
│   └── fonts/              # Custom fonts (optional)
├── .clinerules             # This file
├── netlify.toml            # Netlify deploy config
├── package.json            # Dev dependencies only (Vite)
└── README.md               # Project overview
```

---

## 🛠️ Cline Behavior Expectations

### When I Ask For Changes
1. **Read the file first** — Always check current state before editing
2. **Make targeted edits** — Use replace_in_file for small changes
3. **Test visually** — Suggest checking the browser after changes
4. **Commit often** — Small, descriptive commits
5. **Push to feature branch** — Never push directly to main

### Commit Message Format
```
feat: add winamp music player
fix: correct cursor trail color
style: update neon palette
chore: add music directory
```

### When Something Breaks
1. Check the browser console for errors
2. Verify file paths are correct
3. Test in dev server before committing
4. Keep a backup of working state

